From 7f989e4b95c9c9e336eb023c93ad7d40de56221d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:15:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] dwc2d: USB sticks as a disk scheme (bulk-only transport,
 SCSI)

A bulk-only SCSI interface (class 8, subclass 6, protocol 0x50) found at
boot or plugged in later is set up with INQUIRY, TEST UNIT READY (up to
5 s while the stick gets ready) and READ CAPACITY (10, or 16 above
2 TiB), and served through driver-block's DiskScheme as
disk.usb-dwc2+<ports>-scsi, like upstream's usbscsid: 0 is the whole
stick, 0p0, 0p1, ... its partitions. Reads and writes go out as READ and
WRITE (10, or 16 for large disks) in chunks of up to 64 KiB on host
channels 4 and 5, with the BOT recovery steps for stalls and phase
errors. A stick that stops answering returns ENODEV; when it is unplugged
the scheme goes away.

One stick at a time; a full-speed stick behind a high-speed hub is not
supported (no split bulk transfers).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
